[b]Right-click to play. Use your side buttons to undo.[/b]
Spire Mouse brings mouse controls, adjustable speed, combat Undo/Redo, and room restarts together in one convenience mod for Slay the Spire 2. No prerequisite mods are required.

[h2]Default controls[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Play a card:[/b] Right-click a card that needs no target to play it. For targeted cards, right-click the card, then right-click the target; alternatively, hold the right mouse button, drag to the target, and release.
[*][b]Select cards:[/b] Right-click to select or deselect. Right-click empty space to confirm once the selection requirements are met.
[*][b]End your turn:[/b] Double right-click empty space in combat.
[*][b]Continue:[/b] Right-click empty space after claiming rewards or completing the room's choices. This does not automatically skip unclaimed rewards or required choices.
[*][b]Undo:[/b] Rear thumb button (M4).
[*][b]Redo:[/b] Front thumb button (M5).
[*][b]Restart the room:[/b] Press both thumb buttons together, or press F5.
[*][b]Cancel targeting:[/b] Esc.
[/list]
These are the default bindings. Change them in the game's Settings → Spire Mouse.

[h2]Undo a combat restart, too[/h2]
Undo/Redo card plays, potion use, turn progression, and other recorded combat actions.

[b]Play → Restart → Undo returns to just before the restart → Redo returns to the restarted opening.[/b]

Earlier actions and a pending card selection can also be restored. Taking a new action after Undo replaces the existing redo branch. Restoring across a restart can take longer than an ordinary Undo.

[h2]Speed and settings[/h2]
Open Settings → Spire Mouse to adjust bindings, speed, history capacity, card-selection checkpoints, and the action-history panel. The history panel is hidden by default.

[h2]Scope[/h2]
[list]
[*]Undo/Redo and room restarts are singleplayer features.
[*]Undo/Redo is available during combat. Event choices and returning to a finished combat from its rewards screen are not supported.
[*]You can also restart a non-combat room, but that restart cannot be undone or redone.
[*]History is kept in memory for the current room and does not survive quitting the game.
[/list]

[h2]Tested environment[/h2]
Mod 2.0.0-beta.19 / Windows / game v0.113.1 public-beta. Compatibility with every card, event, and combination of other mods is not guaranteed.

[b]Credits[/b]
